{
  "note": "Which batch actions a message multi-select toolbar may offer right now, and the ids each one reports. The same table runs on four kits (FR-034): the toolbar mirrors ConversationBatchToolbar — the host declares capabilities and the toolbar reports one action with the selected ids.",
  "order": [
    "forwardEach",
    "forwardMerged",
    "pin",
    "pinSelf",
    "delete"
  ],
  "minimumSelection": {
    "forwardMerged": 2
  },
  "forward": {
    "actions": [
      "forwardEach",
      "forwardMerged"
    ],
    "rule": "unforwardableIds (optional, empty by default) are selected ids the core's message.action_availability answers canForward false for — a plugin card that does not declare forwardable. The forward actions count only the forwardable ids (the selection minus unforwardableIds): forwardEach needs at least 1, forwardMerged at least minimumSelection.forwardMerged; each reports only the forwardable ids, in selection order. Every other action counts and reports the whole selection. An id in unforwardableIds that is not selected counts for nothing.",
    "hint": "While the selection holds unforwardable ids the toolbar's meta shows messageBatchUnforwardable(count) (Vue batch.unforwardable): count = the selected ids in unforwardableIds, one form for 1 in English (plural-vectors.json)."
  },
